# seo-drift.sh writes its snapshot state here at runtime (see
# scripts/seo-drift.sh, data/text/seo.md §0 WP-5). Snapshots are
# environment-specific (host-derived canonicals differ between localhost,
# preview, and prod — see seo-drift.sh's path_of_url comment) and are
# regenerated by the first run against whatever base URL you point it at, so
# they don't belong in version control: shipping a committed baseline would
# make the very first run against a *different* host (e.g. prod after
# developing against localhost) misreport a false canonical-drift regression
# instead of establishing a clean baseline.
*
!.gitignore
